tput, which requires its own additional stability and accumulated residual-error analysis.\n\n**Work record.** Count every Jacobian assembly and factorization attempt at a refresh, every linear solve, and, for dense LU, each correction's forward and backward triangular solve. Reuse a chord factorization only for its declared refresh period. Sparse cost depends on the actual stage matrix and backend; this procedure assigns no sparse complexity bound. No general Newton convergence or forward-accuracy claim is part of the algorithm.",
